  "repairs": [
    "Each original RexInputRef is reconstructed once; uses resolve to that exact object across distinct input environments.",
    "Equal distinct original objects remain distinct. Every object/environment pair is type checked, including subsequent uses.",
    "Validation bounds object, environment, producer, edge and pair counts; duplicate states, missing uses, out-of-range references and incompatible rows fail.",
    "The same strict resolved-reference type compatibility is shared by the fragment and input-use Rust validators."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Input owners reference opaque relation/function IDs with supplied rows; producer-row correctness requires the full relation adapter.",
    "This transports RexInputRef objects only; full shared call, lambda, correlation and source-use graphs remain open.",
    "Contexts describe optimized-view inputs and function bodies, not full statement/catalog state.",
    "Full detached S1-to-S2 and P0 remain incomplete."
  ]
